const e="cfc-youth-competitions",l=2011,n="The guideline packet is a 2011 edition for the Pre-Con and Conference. It prints no entry fee, venue, address, contact person, registration steps, prizes, ranks or age minimum. The packet says judge score sheets are at its end, but only the point distributions in the rules were available. Dates are past-edition values kept as a starting suggestion.",o={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"CFC Youth Pre-Con and Conference competitions",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"No one over 22 years of age may compete. All Pre-Con winners advance to the Conference competitions unless otherwise specified.",Notes:["Competitions are placed within Pre-Con and foster fun, fellowship, friendship and faith.","Prepare spiritually through prayer, fasting and the Sacraments of Confession and the Eucharist (encouraged, not required)."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"About the competitions",Items:["Competitions foster fun, fellowship, friendship and faith among brothers and sisters in the community and challenge the youth to excel in the talents God gave them.","The youth use their talents to evangelize and glorify God, so all competitions should exemplify Jesus Christ and be approached in a Christian manner.",'Creative competitions are meant to evangelize and take inspiration from the conference theme from Ephesians 6:10-18, "Put on the Full Armor of God" (Ephesians 6:11).',"Read and be fully competent in all the changes to the rules and regulations. For example, the Individual Original Pieces competition replaces the Sing-Off competition.","For questions on the set-up or execution of the competitions, contact the regional Full-Time Worker, Youth Core Member or Couple Coordinator."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Who may enter",Items:["These are competitions for CFC Youth: no one over the age of 22 is allowed to compete.","No member of a team, cast, production or band may be older than 22 years of age.","Wacky Sports is open to everyone, and coordinators and program volunteers can be included."]},{Key:"levels",Title:"Pre-Con to Conference",Items:["All winners at Pre-Con advance to compete in the Conference competitions, unless otherwise specified.","Amazing Race: winning teams from each region's Pre-Con are placed in a champion's pool and compete against a pool of challengers, who are walk-in competitors at the National Conference. The final race is different but has the same components.","Wacky Sports: there are no national finals, because a new set of wacky sports is held at the National Conference. Any national conference participant can sign up at the start of the National Conference."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"Signing up",Items:["Competitors for Wacky Sports sign up on the day of Pre-Con.","Wacky sports are chosen according to the time, space and other resources available at each Pre-Con, and other games can be added to foster team building and fellowship."]},{Key:"judging",Title:"Judging",Items:["Judges must be competent and have ample experience in the competition being judged, unless the competition does not call for it, such as Wacky Sports.","Judges must have read and fully understand the rules and regulations for their competition and all competitions, for example the age limit.","Judges should be as unbiased as possible. For example, try not to choose Couple Coordinators to judge their own areas.","Make sure judges have all the score sheets they need and fully understand their responsibilities. Choosing judges from the other adult ministries is encouraged.","Follow these requirements, but make the best decision for your region, depending on who attends and is able to judge.","Score sheets for judges are printed at the end of the guidelines packet."]},{Key:"reporting",Title:"Recording and screening",Items:["Original Christian Dance Production: all performances at Pre-Con must be recorded. Regional winners submit the recording from the day of Pre-Con to their Full-Time Worker for screening by the National Youth Core. The deadline is {{DanceRecordingDeadline}}.","Original Christian Dance Production: regions may be asked to perform at the conference site for further screening."]},{Key:"other",Title:"Not modelled",Items:["Wacky Sports is a sign-up fun event with no scoring and is not set up as a scored competition."]}],Documents:[]},t=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"CFC Youth Competitions Rules & Regulations",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Individual Original Pieces and the Evangelistic T-shirt Design are entered by one person."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Individual Original Pieces and the Evangelistic T-shirt Design are entered by one person.`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"CFC Youth Competitions Rules & Regulations",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Team size: Amazing Race 12 members (six of each gender); Original Christian Dance Production 10 to 30 dancers; Defenders of the Faith 3 to 5 members; Band / Original Song 5 to 10 members.","The CFC-Youth Promo Video is made by a production and cast team; no member of the production or cast may be older than 22 years of age."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Team size: Amazing Race 12 members (six of each gender); Original Christian Dance Production 10 to 30 dancers; Defenders of the Faith 3 to 5 members; Band / Original Song 5 to 10 members.
- The CFC-Youth Promo Video is made by a production and cast team; no member of the production or cast may be older than 22 years of age.`}],a=[],i=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Amazing Race","Source":"Amazing Race","Sections":{"About":["Competitors are led through an intense race and obstacle course.","The key components are Athleticism, Team Building, Problem Solving, Decision Making, Academics, Bible/Catholic Trivia and Miscellaneous Obstacles."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Each team has 12 members, six of each gender.","No one on the team can be older than 22 years of age.","Local areas are encouraged to create an amazing race that has all seven key components.","The final Amazing Race at the National Conference is different but has the same components."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The team that completes the course in the shortest time, fulfilling every requirement of every station, wins."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Competitors are led through an intense race and obstacle course.\\n- The key components are Athleticism, Team Building, Problem Solving, Decision Making, Academics, Bible/Catholic Trivia and Miscellaneous Obstacles.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each team has 12 members, six of each gender.\\n- No one on the team can be older than 22 years of age.\\n- Local areas are encouraged to create an amazing race that has all seven key components.\\n- The final Amazing Race at the National Conference is different but has the same components.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The team that completes the course in the shortest time, fulfilling every requirement of every station, wins."},{"Title":"Original Christian Dance Production","Source":"Original Christian Dance Production","Sections":{"About":["A production meant to glorify God in a dynamic, inspirational way, more than a mere dance, that could be performed before clergy, couple coordinators or parents and at high schools, college campuses and parishes.","The youth incorporate a piece of the Armor of God from Ephesians 6:10-18 (belt of truth, breastplate of righteousness, shoes of the Gospel of peace, shield of faith, helmet of salvation, sword of the Spirit). The theme should be seen in the music, choreography, storyline and costumes.","One piece of armor is assigned to each region; the Full-Time Worker of the region advises the assignments."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum time 4 minutes, starting as soon as the music begins.","1 point is deducted from the total score for each second over the 4-minute limit.","A minimum of 10 and a maximum of 30 dancers may perform. For a smaller stage, be ready to adjust routines on the day, for example some dancers on the floor."],"Rules":["Each performance must incorporate the armor piece assigned to it.","It is a production and cannot be purely dance.","All performances must be Christian and of an inspiring nature.","No one in the presentation can be older than 22 years of age.","A mix of 3 to 5 songs (medley) can be used. Secular songs can be included, but one song must be Christian or inspirational. Suggestive lyrics are not allowed.","Music is accepted only on a CD in audio format, with ONE song on the CD, labeled with the area's name on the front.","Props and elaborate costumes are encouraged.","The performance on the day of Conference must be the one performed at Pre-Con. Major changes warrant point deduction or disqualification.","What is worn at Pre-Con is what is worn at the National Conference. Points are deducted or a disqualification may follow if costumes do not match."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Any suggestive or inappropriate moves, lyrics or clothing automatically disqualifies the presentation. All performances must be 100% pure from start to finish."],"Judging":["The National Youth Core and Full-Time Workers may eliminate competitors for indecent or immodest attire, music or choreography at any time during a performance.","Printed point distribution (adds up to 105): Execution 30, Relatedness to Theme 25, Creativity 15, Originality 10, Costumes 10, Crowd reaction 10, Song selections 5."],"Points":null,"Notes":["The winner may be asked to perform the production for clergy during the conference."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A production meant to glorify God in a dynamic, inspirational way, more than a mere dance, that could be performed before clergy, couple coordinators or parents and at high schools, college campuses and parishes.\\n- The youth incorporate a piece of the Armor of God from Ephesians 6:10-18 (belt of truth, breastplate of righteousness, shoes of the Gospel of peace, shield of faith, helmet of salvation, sword of the Spirit). The theme should be seen in the music, choreography, storyline and costumes.\\n- One piece of armor is assigned to each region; the Full-Time Worker of the region advises the assignments.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum time 4 minutes, starting as soon as the music begins.\\n- 1 point is deducted from the total score for each second over the 4-minute limit.\\n- A minimum of 10 and a maximum of 30 dancers may perform. For a smaller stage, be ready to adjust routines on the day, for example some dancers on the floor.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each performance must incorporate the armor piece assigned to it.\\n- It is a production and cannot be purely dance.\\n- All performances must be Christian and of an inspiring nature.\\n- No one in the presentation can be older than 22 years of age.\\n- A mix of 3 to 5 songs (medley) can be used. Secular songs can be included, but one song must be Christian or inspirational. Suggestive lyrics are not allowed.\\n- Music is accepted only on a CD in audio format, with ONE song on the CD, labeled with the area's name on the front.\\n- Props and elaborate costumes are encouraged.\\n- The performance on the day of Conference must be the one performed at Pre-Con. Major changes warrant point deduction or disqualification.\\n- What is worn at Pre-Con is what is worn at the National Conference. Points are deducted or a disqualification may follow if costumes do not match.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Any suggestive or inappropriate moves, lyrics or clothing automatically disqualifies the presentation. All performances must be 100% pure from start to finish.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The National Youth Core and Full-Time Workers may eliminate competitors for indecent or immodest attire, music or choreography at any time during a performance.\\n- Printed point distribution (adds up to 105): Execution 30, Relatedness to Theme 25, Creativity 15, Originality 10, Costumes 10, Crowd reaction 10, Song selections 5.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The winner may be asked to perform the production for clergy during the conference."},{"Title":"Defenders of the Faith","Source":"Defenders of the Faith","Sections":{"About":["Prepares leaders for real-life instances where their beliefs are questioned. Questions are chosen to catechize the youth of the region."],"TimeAndFormat":["There are three rounds. Each team has 3 minutes to confer and present its answer in the final round."],"Rules":["Teams have 3 to 5 members and no one can be older than 22 years of age.","Questions about the Catholic Faith are True/False, Short Answer and Multiple Choice. The moderator asks all questions while the judges provide the scores.","Categories are The Gospels, The Holy Mass, The Sacraments and Social Justice (for example Pro-Life) issues, with FIVE questions in each category.","Round one covers The Holy Mass and The Gospels. Round two covers The Sacraments and Social Justice.","In rounds one and two, the first group chooses a question from a category. The moderator reads the whole question and the group that buzzes in first answers. Only one person answers and teammates may not confer.","Every team member must be given a chance to answer at least once before anyone answers twice.","The third round, The Final Judgment, has one question: every team defends itself against a scenario where its beliefs are challenged.","Each team may bring and use its own Bible and the Catechism of the Catholic Church during the whole competition."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The team with the most points at the end wins.","All questions and answers are judged on accuracy against the Bible and the Catechism of the Catholic Church. Judges knowledgeable of both should be on hand."],"Points":["Round one: 2 points for every correct answer.","Round two: 4 points for every correct answer.","A wrong answer in rounds one and two loses 1 point from the team's score.","Final Judgment on a scale of 1-10: 10 points for the most accurate answer, 5 points for a semi-accurate answer, 0 for a wrong answer."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Prepares leaders for real-life instances where their beliefs are questioned. Questions are chosen to catechize the youth of the region.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- There are three rounds. Each team has 3 minutes to confer and present its answer in the final round.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Teams have 3 to 5 members and no one can be older than 22 years of age.\\n- Questions about the Catholic Faith are True/False, Short Answer and Multiple Choice. The moderator asks all questions while the judges provide the scores.\\n- Categories are The Gospels, The Holy Mass, The Sacraments and Social Justice (for example Pro-Life) issues, with FIVE questions in each category.\\n- Round one covers The Holy Mass and The Gospels. Round two covers The Sacraments and Social Justice.\\n- In rounds one and two, the first group chooses a question from a category. The moderator reads the whole question and the group that buzzes in first answers. Only one person answers and teammates may not confer.\\n- Every team member must be given a chance to answer at least once before anyone answers twice.\\n- The third round, The Final Judgment, has one question: every team defends itself against a scenario where its beliefs are challenged.\\n- Each team may bring and use its own Bible and the Catechism of the Catholic Church during the whole competition.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The team with the most points at the end wins.\\n- All questions and answers are judged on accuracy against the Bible and the Catechism of the Catholic Church. Judges knowledgeable of both should be on hand.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Round one: 2 points for every correct answer.\\n- Round two: 4 points for every correct answer.\\n- A wrong answer in rounds one and two loses 1 point from the team's score.\\n- Final Judgment on a scale of 1-10: 10 points for the most accurate answer, 5 points for a semi-accurate answer, 0 for a wrong answer."},{"Title":"Band / Original Song","Source":"Band/Original Song","Sections":{"About":["Youth are encouraged to grow in creating original songs for the community. Winners at conference may have their songs used in one of the conference worships."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each band has 8 minutes for the whole presentation, including at most 1 minute of sharing what inspired the composition (introduction videos if necessary).","1 point is deducted from the total score for each second over the time limit.","The remaining 7 minutes are for one original praise and worship song and one original reflection song."],"Rules":["No fewer than 5 and no more than 10 people in the band.","Instruments are not limited to acoustic/electric guitar, keyboard, bass and drums (for example percussion and wind instruments are allowed). Notify the organisers of exactly what instruments and props will be used.","Areas bring their own instruments; the host area provides the drum set.","All entries relate to the theme \\"Put on the FULL Armor of God\\" (Ephesians 6:11).","Written music must be positive and/or Christian, Christ-centered and clean, with no negative language or slang.","No additional dancers or non-band members may be added during the performance.","Five typed copies of the song lyrics are required on the day, showing the song names, all band member names and region/area."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["Printed point distribution: Creativity & Originality 20, Musical arrangement/Transitions 20, Unified as a band (vocals) 25, Instruments Utilized 15, Audience Impact/Crowd Rapport 10, Relatedness to Theme 10."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Youth are encouraged to grow in creating original songs for the community. Winners at conference may have their songs used in one of the conference worships.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each band has 8 minutes for the whole presentation, including at most 1 minute of sharing what inspired the composition (introduction videos if necessary).\\n- 1 point is deducted from the total score for each second over the time limit.\\n- The remaining 7 minutes are for one original praise and worship song and one original reflection song.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- No fewer than 5 and no more than 10 people in the band.\\n- Instruments are not limited to acoustic/electric guitar, keyboard, bass and drums (for example percussion and wind instruments are allowed). Notify the organisers of exactly what instruments and props will be used.\\n- Areas bring their own instruments; the host area provides the drum set.\\n- All entries relate to the theme \\"Put on the FULL Armor of God\\" (Ephesians 6:11).\\n- Written music must be positive and/or Christian, Christ-centered and clean, with no negative language or slang.\\n- No additional dancers or non-band members may be added during the performance.\\n- Five typed copies of the song lyrics are required on the day, showing the song names, all band member names and region/area.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Printed point distribution: Creativity & Originality 20, Musical arrangement/Transitions 20, Unified as a band (vocals) 25, Instruments Utilized 15, Audience Impact/Crowd Rapport 10, Relatedness to Theme 10."},{"Title":"Individual Original Pieces","Source":"Individual Original Pieces","Sections":{"About":["An opportunity for individual artists to share God's glory in a simple original song or spoken word/poetry. No band is necessary.","Chosen original songs and spoken word/poetry pieces are compiled onto one CD with chosen pieces from all over the nation."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each piece can be at most 5 minutes long."],"Rules":["All entries relate to the theme \\"Put on the Full Armor of God\\" (Ephesians 6:11).","Original pieces must be positive and/or Christian, Christ-centered and clean, with no negative language or slang.","No additional dancers or non-band members may be added during the performance.","Five typed copies of the lyrics are required on the day, with the title of the piece, the name and region/area."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["Printed point distribution: Creativity 30, Originality 30, Delivery 20, Relatedness to Theme 15, Crowd Reaction 5."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- An opportunity for individual artists to share God's glory in a simple original song or spoken word/poetry. No band is necessary.\\n- Chosen original songs and spoken word/poetry pieces are compiled onto one CD with chosen pieces from all over the nation.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each piece can be at most 5 minutes long.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- All entries relate to the theme \\"Put on the Full Armor of God\\" (Ephesians 6:11).\\n- Original pieces must be positive and/or Christian, Christ-centered and clean, with no negative language or slang.\\n- No additional dancers or non-band members may be added during the performance.\\n- Five typed copies of the lyrics are required on the day, with the title of the piece, the name and region/area.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Printed point distribution: Creativity 30, Originality 30, Delivery 20, Relatedness to Theme 15, Crowd Reaction 5."},{"Title":"CFC-Youth Promo Video","Source":"CFC-Youth Promo Video","Sections":{"About":["Youth create a promotional video to show to parishes or campuses: a 75-second commercial showing what the ministry has to offer.","The video should introduce people unfamiliar with CFC Youth to its life, membership, values and beliefs, and attract and invite newcomers to events such as camps."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each video cannot exceed 75 seconds. 1 point is deducted from the total score for each second over the limit."],"Rules":["Members of the production and the cast cannot be older than 22 years of age."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["Printed point distribution: Creativity & Originality 30 (how original and creative is the video), Clarity of message 30 (is the message clearly presented for the intended audience), Impact 15 (does it leave a lasting impression and spur action), Christ-Centered 25 (does it show the central focus of CFC Youth)."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Youth create a promotional video to show to parishes or campuses: a 75-second commercial showing what the ministry has to offer.\\n- The video should introduce people unfamiliar with CFC Youth to its life, membership, values and beliefs, and attract and invite newcomers to events such as camps.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each video cannot exceed 75 seconds. 1 point is deducted from the total score for each second over the limit.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Members of the production and the cast cannot be older than 22 years of age.\\n\\n## Points\\n- Printed point distribution: Creativity & Originality 30 (how original and creative is the video), Clarity of message 30 (is the message clearly presented for the intended audience), Impact 15 (does it leave a lasting impression and spur action), Christ-Centered 25 (does it show the central focus of CFC Youth)."},{"Title":"Evangelistic T-shirt Design","Source":"Evangelistic T-shirt Design","Sections":{"About":["A shirt design that sparks conversation and evangelizes to peers and strangers. This year there is no regional shirt and the details of conference are not added; the Bible verse may be added."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Shirts represent CFC Youth as a whole and are designed to spark interest from strangers.","The shirt has a Christian-based theme that may indicate the Conference verse \\"Put on the Full Armor of God\\" (Ephesians 6:11).","The base color of the shirt is green camouflage.","Designs may be printed on both sides, but this is not required.","Designs cannot have more than 3 colors per side.","Entrants cannot be older than 22 years of age.","Present the design digitally or printed on paper, with the right background color for the assigned shirt color.","Hand in (a) on paper with an explanation of the logo, AND (b) saved as an image file burned on a CD (the guideline prints the file type as \\".pang\\")."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":["Printed point distribution (adds up to 50): Creativity 20, Originality 20, Wearability 5, Requirements met 5."],"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A shirt design that sparks conversation and evangelizes to peers and strangers. This year there is no regional shirt and the details of conference are not added; the Bible verse may be added.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Shirts represent CFC Youth as a whole and are designed to spark interest from strangers.\\n- The shirt has a Christian-based theme that may indicate the Conference verse \\"Put on the Full Armor of God\\" (Ephesians 6:11).\\n- The base color of the shirt is green camouflage.\\n- Designs may be printed on both sides, but this is not required.\\n- Designs cannot have more than 3 colors per side.\\n- Entrants cannot be older than 22 years of age.\\n- Present the design digitally or printed on paper, with the right background color for the assigned shirt color.\\n- Hand in (a) on paper with an explanation of the logo, AND (b) saved as an image file burned on a CD (the guideline prints the file type as \\".pang\\").\\n\\n## Points\\n- Printed point distribution (adds up to 50): Creativity 20, Originality 20, Wearability 5, Requirements met 5."}]`),s=[],r=[{Key:"DanceRecordingDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Dance recording submission deadline",Value:"2011-07-01 5pm PST / 8pm EST",Source:"Original Christian Dance Production, note to regional winners (2011 edition)"}],d=[{Claim:"Rules and regulations of the CFC Youth Pre-Con and Conference competitions as printed by the organiser.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"CFC Youth Competitions Rules & Regulations",Url:"https://www.scribd.com/document/55444127/CFC-Youth-Competition-Guidelines"}],h={TemplateKey:e,Year:2011,Note:n,Page:o,ParticipantTypes:t,AgeGroups:a,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:d};export{a as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,d as Evidence,n as Note,o as Page,t as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,l as Year,h as default};
